Article 3 Where property for payment in kind under the preceding Article is delivered, the head of the tax office shall handle it as follows:
1. Real property: Request the competent registry office to register the transfer of ownership of the real property;
2. Securities:
  (a) For government bonds, immediately cancel unregistered government bonds; for registered government bonds, take procedures to request registration of change in the name of the Minister of Finance pursuant to Articles 29 and 30 of the Enforcement Decree of the Government Bonds Act and cancel the notice of completion of registration under Article 41 of that Decree. Where the relevant government bonds are registered in the Class B Government Bond Register, attach the relevant government bond certificates;
  (b) For public bonds and other securities, immediately cancel bearer securities; for registered securities, have the taxpayer take procedures to request a change into the name of the Minister of Finance and cancel them after attaching documents evidencing the change.
